  "id": "Kingston-22_03513_FUL",
  "description": "Replacement of single-glazing windows with double-glazing windows",
  "decision_date": "30/01/2023",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall be commenced within 3 years from the date of this decision.\r\rReason: In order to comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act, 1990.  (As amended)\r",
    "The colour of the outward facing frames to be used for the replacement windows shall be dark brown in order to match existing and those of neighbouring properties in Wellington Court and shall thereafter be retained as such.\r\rReason: To ensure a satisfactory appearance on completion of the development in accordance with Policy DM10 (Design Requirements for New Developments including House Extensions) of the LDF Core Strategy Adopted April 2012.\r",
    "The replacement windows hereby permitted shall be implemented in such a way as to match the existing depths of reveals and to preserve the existing masonry and brickwork and shall thereafter be retained as such.\r\rReason:  To ensure a satisfactory appearance on completion of the development in accordance with Policy DM10 (Design Requirements for New Developments including House Extensions) of the LDF Core Strategy Adopted April 2012.\r"
  ],
  "development_type": "Minor dwellings"
